quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  17,105,"And with the truth, We have revealed it (i.e. the Qur’an), and with the truth, it has come down. And (O Prophet!) We have not sent you except as a Bearer of glad tidings and as a Warner."
  17,106,"(It is) a Qur’an, We have divided it into distinct parts so that you may recite it to the people in intervals. And We have sent it down in successive revelations."
  17,107,"Say: ‘Believe in it or do not believe.’ Indeed, those who were given knowledge before it, when it is recited to them, fall on their faces in prostration."
  17,108,"And they say: ‘Glory be to our Lord. Indeed, our Lord’s promise is fulfilled.’"
  17,109,"And they fall down upon their faces weeping, and it (i.e. the Qur’an) increases them in humility."
  17,110,"Say: ‘Invoke Allah or invoke al-Rahman (the Most Compassionate). Whichever (Name) you call, to Him belong the Most Beautiful Names.’ And be not loud in your prayer, nor too quiet in it; instead, seek a middle course between the two."
  17,111,"And say: ‘All praise belongs to Allah, Who has never taken any son nor does He have any partner in the kingdom; nor has He (taken) any helper out of weakness.’ And proclaim His Greatness with a magnification (worthy of Him)."
  18,1,"All praise belongs to Allah, Who revealed the Book to His (Esteemed) Servant and did not allow any deviation to be in it."
  18,2,"(He has made it) perfectly upright, to warn (the disbelievers) of severe punishment from Him and to give glad tidings to the believers who perform righteous deeds that there shall be a beautiful reward for them,"
  18,3,"wherein they shall stay forever,"
  18,4,and to warn those who say: ‘Allah has taken a son.’
